Topic 23 – Collections Framework
Objective: Collection operations, iteration, collection methods, sorting, removal and traversal.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Collection Overview	Create an ArrayList and add, retrieve and display elements.
02	Add and Remove	Add multiple elements to a collection and remove selected elements.
03	Contains and Size	Check whether an element exists and display the collection size.
04	Iteration	Iterate through a collection using for loop, enhanced for loop and Iterator.
05	Sorting	Sort a collection of integers in ascending and descending order.
06	Duplicate Elements	Store duplicate values in a List and observe the results.
07	Remove Duplicates	Convert a List into a Set and display unique values.
08	Collection Comparison	Compare two collections and find common elements.
09	List Modification	Add, update, remove and retrieve elements from a List.
10	Test Case Collection	Store test case names in a collection, sort them and remove completed test cases.



Topic 24 – List, Set, Map and Queue
Objective: Understand ArrayList, LinkedList, HashSet, LinkedHashSet, HashMap and Queue operations.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	ArrayList	Create an ArrayList of test case names and perform add, update, retrieve and remove operations.
02	LinkedList	Create a LinkedList of tasks and demonstrate insertion and deletion at different positions.
03	HashSet	Store duplicate values in a HashSet and observe how duplicates are handled.
04	LinkedHashSet	Store values in a LinkedHashSet and observe insertion order and duplicate handling.
05	HashMap	Store employee IDs as keys and employee names as values. Retrieve values using keys.
06	Map Iteration	Iterate through a HashMap using entrySet, keySet and values.
07	Queue	Create a Queue and demonstrate offer(), poll() and peek().
08	PriorityQueue	Create a PriorityQueue of integers and observe the order in which elements are retrieved.
09	Collections Comparison	Store duplicate and unique values using List and Set. Compare their behaviour.
10	QA Test Data Management	Use a Map to store username and password, a List to store test cases and a Set to store unique test results.